.TH SLURM-GPU 1 "February 2026" "slurm-gpu 0.1.0" "Slurm GPU Reporting"
.SH NAME
slurm-gpu \- GPU utilization reporting for Slurm clusters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slurm-gpu
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B slurm-report
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B slurm-usage
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B slurm-stat
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B slurm-show-tres
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slurm-gpu
queries Slurm accounting data (sacct), node configuration (scontrol), and
job queues (squeue) to produce GPU utilization reports, cluster-wide usage
summaries, and real-time job monitoring statistics.
.PP
The binary supports symlink dispatch: creating symlinks named
.BR slurm-report ,
.BR slurm-usage ,
.BR slurm-stat ,
or
.B slurm-show-tres
pointing to
.B slurm-gpu
invokes the corresponding subcommand automatically.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B report
Generate GPU utilization reports from sacct job data. Shows per-job
efficiency metrics with optional time-weighted averages, summaries, and
Telegraf output.
.TP
.B usage
Show current GPU availability by type across the cluster. Supports
per-user breakdowns and Telegraf output.
.TP
.B stat
Monitor currently running jobs with real-time GPU and CPU statistics
using sstat.
.TP
.B show-tres
Display the dynamic TRES (Trackable Resource) ID-to-name mappings
configured on the cluster.
.SH REPORT OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-starttime " " \fITIME\fR
Start time for sacct query. Accepts dates (2026-01-15), relative
keywords (yesterday, today), or Slurm time formats.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-endtime " " \fITIME\fR
End time for sacct query.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-partition " " \fIPARTITION\fR
Filter jobs by Slurm partition.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-account " " \fIACCOUNT\fR
Filter jobs by Slurm account (comma-separated list).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
Query a specific user. Enables the time-weighted average row.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-allusers
Query all users.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIJOBIDS\fR
Comma-separated list of specific job IDs to query.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gpu
Only show jobs that request GPU resources.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu\-idle
Show only jobs with GPU utilization < 50% or GPU memory efficiency < 50%.
.TP
.B \-\-summary
Generate summary report grouped by user.
.TP
.B \-\-summary\-by\-partition
Generate summary report grouped by user and partition.
.TP
.B \-\-summary\-by\-account
Generate summary report grouped by user and account.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Include node, GPU type, and account columns.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Use plain text output instead of rich formatting.
.TP
.B \-\-telegraf
Output time-weighted average efficiency metrics in InfluxDB Line Protocol
format for Telegraf ingestion. When used with
.BR \-u ,
outputs a single line for that user. When used with
.BR \-a ,
outputs one line per user. Ignored when combined with
.B \-\-summary*
flags.
.IP
Measurement name:
.BR slurm_gpu_efficiency .
Tags: user (always), partition (if
.B \-r
specified), account (if
.B \-A
specified). Fields: cpu_eff, mem_eff, gpu_eff, gpu_util, gpu_mem_eff, gpu_mem.
Fields with no data default to 0.0 so every line has a consistent field set
(required by Prometheus).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write report to file instead of stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-filter\-state " " \fISTATE\fR
Filter jobs by state: all, completed, failed, pending, running.
Default: all.
.TP
.BR \-\-min\-gpu\-eff " " \fIVALUE\fR
Only show jobs with GPU efficiency >= this value.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of jobs to display.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-by " " \fIFIELD\fR
Sort by: user, job_id, state, elapsed, gpu_eff, gpu_mem_eff, time_eff,
cpu_eff, mem_eff. Default: job_id.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-partition
Include partition column in the report. Default: true.
.SH USAGE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Show detailed report with node names.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-partition " " \fIPARTITION\fR
Show only nodes in the specified partition(s). Comma-separated.
.TP
.B \-k
Shortcut for partitions: h200ea,education,gpu-common,scavenger-gpu.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
Show GPU usage for a specific user.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show GPU usage breakdown by all users.
.TP
.B \-\-telegraf
Output in InfluxDB Line Protocol format for Telegraf. Measurement name:
.BR slurm_gpu_usage .
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output.
.SH STAT OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Include node and GPU type columns.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
Specific user to query. Auto-filters to current user for non-root.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-partition " " \fIPARTITION\fR
Filter by Slurm partition.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIJOBIDS\fR
Comma-separated list of specific job IDs.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of jobs to display. Default: 50.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-by " " \fIFIELD\fR
Sort by: user, job_id, elapsed, gpu_eff, gpu_mem_eff, time_eff,
cpu_eff, mem_eff. Default: job_id.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output.
.SH REPORT COLUMNS
.SS Job Reports
.TP
.B User
Job owner.
.TP
.B JobID
Slurm job identifier.
.TP
.B State
Job state (COMPLETED, FAILED, RUNNING, CANCELLED, TIMEOUT, etc.).
.TP
.B Elapsed
Job runtime in HH:MM:SS format.
.TP
.B TimeEff
Time efficiency: elapsed time / time limit.
.TP
.B CPUEff
CPU efficiency: CPU time used / CPU time allocated.
.TP
.B MemEff
Memory efficiency: peak memory / allocated memory.
.TP
.B GPUEff
GPU efficiency: normalized per-GPU average utilization.
.TP
.B GPUUtil
Peak GPU utilization percentage (total across all GPUs).
.TP
.B GPUMemEff
GPU memory efficiency: GPU memory used / total GPU memory capacity.
.TP
.B GPUMem
Peak GPU memory usage.
.TP
.B Partition
Slurm partition name.
.SS Time-Weighted Average
When filtering by a specific user (\fB\-u\fR), a WEIGHTED AVERAGE row
appears at the bottom. Each metric is weighted by job elapsed time:
.PP
.nf
  weighted_avg = sum(elapsed_time * value) / sum(elapsed_time)
.fi
.PP
Longer-running jobs have proportionally more influence on the average.
.SH TELEGRAF INTEGRATION
The \fB\-\-telegraf\fR flag on both
.B report
and
.B usage
subcommands outputs data in InfluxDB Line Protocol. This allows direct
ingestion by Telegraf using the
.B exec
input plugin.
.SS Example: Per-User Efficiency (report)
.PP
.nf
  [[inputs.exec]]
    commands = [
      "slurm-gpu report --telegraf -a -S yesterday -E today"
    ]
    data_format = "influx"
    interval = "1h"
.fi
.PP
Produces lines like:
.PP
.nf
  slurm_gpu_efficiency,user=ukh cpu_eff=1.3,mem_eff=59.9,gpu_eff=100.0,gpu_util=100.0,gpu_mem_eff=89.7,gpu_mem=125.6 1738800000000000000
.fi
.SS Example: Cluster GPU Slots (usage)
.PP
.nf
  [[inputs.exec]]
    commands = ["slurm-gpu usage --telegraf"]
    data_format = "influx"
    interval = "5m"
.fi
.PP
Produces lines like:
.PP
.nf
  slurm_gpu_usage,gpu_type=h200 total=16i,used=12i,available=4i,utilization=75.00,node_count=2i 1738800000000000000
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Review yesterday's GPU jobs for a user:
.B slurm-report -u jdoe -S yesterday -g
.TP
Find jobs wasting GPUs:
.B slurm-report --gpu-idle --sort-by gpu_eff -S yesterday
.TP
Cluster GPU availability:
.B slurm-usage --detailed
.TP
Monitor your running jobs:
.B slurm-stat --detailed
.TP
Telegraf output for a user over a day:
.B slurm-report --telegraf -u ukh -r h200alloc -S 2026-02-03 -E 2026-02-04
.TP
Telegraf output for all users:
.B slurm-report --telegraf -a -S yesterday
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B slurm-gpu
requires that Slurm commands
.BR sacct (1),
.BR scontrol (1),
and
.BR squeue (1)
are available in the PATH.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (sacct failure, no matching jobs, I/O error).
